    "result": "## Summary\n\nI fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` wasn't creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Problem:** The frai CLI's `gate` command handler was only passing positional arguments to frai-gate via Commander's variadic `[args...]` capture, but not the option flags like `--ci`. These were being parsed by Commander but never forwarded to the spawned frai-gate process.\n\n**The Solution:** Changed the gate command to use `process.argv` to capture all arguments after 'gate', preserving both positional arguments and flags. This ensures the `--ci` flag reaches frai-gate.\n\n**Verification:** \n- Rebuilt the package: \u2713\n- Tested `frai gate init --ci` \u2192 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` now created \u2713",
